{"node":{"id":"HP:0001331","label":"Absent septum pellucidum","ic":5.53,"definition":"Absence of the septum pellucidum (meaning translucent wall in Latin - SP), also known as the ventricle of Sylvius. The septum pellucidum is a thin, triangular double membrane separating the frontal horns of the right and left lateral ventricles of the brain. It extends between the anterior portion of the corpus callosum, and the body of the fornix and its width varies from 1.5 to 3.0 mm."},"diseases":[{"id":"MONDO:0010466","label":"multiple congenital anomalies-hypotonia-seizures syndrome 2","in_core":false,"edge":{"id":"e_95ce0aa1064e","source":"MONDO:0010466","target":"HP:0001331","type":"has_phenotype","evidence":[{"db":"HPO","origin":"OMIM","record":"OMIM:300868 · PMID:22305531","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/22305531/","level":"observed","date":"2022-08-13","confidence":1.0,"snippet":"Multiple congenital anomalies-hypotonia-seizures syndrome 2: Absent septum pellucidum (frequency 1/1) [PCS]"}],"contradicting":[],"confidence":1.0,"independent_sources":["OMIM"],"level":"observed"},"confidence":1.0},{"id":"MONDO:0008428","label":"septooptic dysplasia","in_core":false,"edge":{"id":"e_6b79d69c8e40","source":"MONDO:0008428","target":"HP:0001331","type":"has_phenotype","evidence":[{"db":"HPO","origin":"OMIM","record":"OMIM:182230 · OMIM:182230","url":"https://omim.org/entry/182230","level":"curated","date":"2012-04-04","confidence":0.5,"snippet":"Septooptic dysplasia: Absent septum pellucidum [PCS]"},{"db":"HPO","origin":"Orphanet","record":"ORPHA:3157 · ORPHA:3157","url":"https://www.orpha.net/en/disease/detail/3157","level":"curated","date":"2026-09-02","confidence":0.6,"snippet":"Septo-optic dysplasia spectrum: Absent septum pellucidum (frequency HP:0040282) [TAS]"},{"db":"Orphanet","origin":"Orphanet","record":"ORPHA:3157","level":"curated","date":"2026-06-23","url":"https://www.orpha.net/en/disease/detail/3157","confidence":0.6,"snippet":"Absent septum pellucidum — Frequ